  "id": "difference-score",
  "term": "difference score",
  "definition": "A difference score is the value obtained by subtracting one measurement from another, so the analysis focuses on the change or discrepancy between them. In correlated or repeated-measures data, these scores are treated as a variable of their own and can be tested against zero or summarized by their mean and standard deviation.",
